  "scope": "Repairs the AUTOINCREMENT high-water mark for SQLite INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT. Committed puts and committed deletes retain the monotonic counter; rollback discards only transaction-local puts and restores the counter to the maximum ID ever committed before that transaction. The final un-specified insert allocates high + 1.",
  "change": "In the rollback branch, compute transaction-local IDs as pending minus committed, clear pending, then recompute high from committed IDs and those rolled-back IDs. This fixes cases such as begin/put 9/rollback returning 1 and put 3/begin/put 11/rollback returning 4, while preserving all previously correct put, delete, begin, commit, and open-transaction outcomes."
